  "statement": "Let $a=\\\\sqrt[3]{9+\\\\sqrt{80}}+\\\\sqrt[3]{9-\\\\sqrt{80}}$. By writing $u=\\\\sqrt[3]{9+\\\\sqrt{80}}$ and $v=\\\\sqrt[3]{9-\\\\sqrt{80}}$, show that $a$ satisfies $a^{3}-3a-18=0$, and hence find the exact value of $a$.",
  "solution": "Let $u=\\\\sqrt[3]{9+\\\\sqrt{80}}$ and $v=\\\\sqrt[3]{9-\\\\sqrt{80}}$. Then $uv=\\\\sqrt[3]{(9+\\\\sqrt{80})(9-\\\\sqrt{80})}=\\\\sqrt[3]{81-80}=\\\\sqrt[3]{1}=1$, and $u^{3}+v^{3}=(9+\\\\sqrt{80})+(9-\\\\sqrt{80})=18$. Now $a^{3}=(u+v)^{3}=u^{3}+v^{3}+3uv(u+v)=18+3(1)a=18+3a$, so $a^{3}-3a-18=0$. Testing $a=3$ gives $27-9-18=0$, so $(a-3)(a^{2}+3a+6)=0$. The quadratic factor has discriminant $9-24<0$, so the only real root is $a=3$.",
